    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2FK94NRG8x7zRDHP6w2r8ca)_\n\nSia reports that the svg-tag-mode integration of #254 blocks Emacs init and overflows memory. This removes it so startup is unblocked first:\n\n- Removes the \"SVG tags in the org buffer\" section from `sp-org-tag-groups.org`, re-tangles `sp-org-tag-groups.el` (nothing left of `sp-org-svg-tags-*`), drops the 4 tests and moves the CHANGELOG line to a removal entry.\n- `sp-org-tag-groups` returns to the pre-#254 version, so the tag colours, emoji and the `--explicit-groups` fix stay. `sp-faces.el` is untouched.\n\n**Cause is not confirmed** (no graphic Emacs here). Likely suspect: `sp-faces.el` already declares `svg-tag-mode` with `use-package` (`:hook prog-mode`, a global `svg-tag-tags`), and #254 declared and enabled it a second time from a late module, with a global mode and a buffer-local `svg-tag-tags`. The next attempt will be stock `svg-tag-mode` only, reusing the `sp-faces` declaration, off by default, with no coupling to the tag groups or emoji and no decoration of file-header tags or TODO keywords.\n\nTests: the 5 remaining ERT tests of the module pass in Emacs 29.3 batch.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNi9xYXWjL6cySxZHmKU)_",
    "changed_files": 4,
    "closed_at": "2026-11-02T17:07:22Z",
    "comment_data": [],
    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "OWNER",
            "body": "The `tangle` check is red only because `libraries/modules/base/navi/sp-search.el` differs from its doc. That file is already out of sync on `main` and this PR doesn't touch it. #253 fixes it, so this PR's own modules pass. `build` and `markers` are green. Merging this PR is not blocked by `tangle` for any reason of its own.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
